## 3. Target Audience & Searcher Profile

The primary searcher is a **renter with one or more pets** who is actively reviewing a lease or preparing to sign one, most likely a young professional or household in the comparison or decision stage of their rental search. They have encountered at least two of three terms (pet fee, pet deposit, pet rent) in a lease or listing and are confused about whether any of that money is returnable. They expect a fast, direct answer that tells them the difference in plain terms, gives them concrete dollar ranges, and helps them evaluate which charge structure is better for their situation. They are not looking for a landlord strategy guide.

