*Writing instruction: This section is legally required for completeness and also targets the PAA question about service animals. State clearly: under the federal Fair Housing Act, landlords cannot charge a pet deposit, pet fee, or pet rent for a verified service animal or emotional support animal. Renters with a valid ESA letter from a licensed healthcare provider should not be charged any pet-related fees. They can still be held responsible for actual damage through the standard security deposit. Keep to one short paragraph. Do not editorialize about fraud or documentation requirements.*

